---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const noSlash = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const u = (p: string) => `${noSlash}${p}`;
---

<ContentLayout
  title="How We Work: Weeks, Not Months | Freedom45"
  description="What it's like to work with Freedom45, from the first call to long after launch: a clear proposal, something real to try within weeks, and the same people looking after it."
  activePage="how-we-work"
>
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
    <h1>Weeks, <span class="g">not months.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Most software doesn't fail because of the code. It fails because nobody found out early enough what its users actually needed. So we put something real in front of people fast, then build on what works.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>Working with us, step by step</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <h3>A conversation</h3>
          <p>Tell us what you're trying to do. We'll ask the awkward questions early and tell you straight if we're not the right fit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <h3>A clear proposal</h3>
          <p>What we'll build first, how long it should take and what it costs, in plain English. No jargon, no padding.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <h3>Something real, early</h3>
          <p>Within weeks you have a working version in front of real users. You see what works before the big spend, and decide what comes next.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <h3>Built in short steps</h3>
          <p>We build in short cycles, with something new you can open and try each time. You're never waiting on a big reveal.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-n" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <h3>Launch, and looked after</h3>
          <p>We host it, support it and keep improving it for as long as you want us to, with the same people who built it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:1.25rem">What we can do at each stage, from prototypes to fractional CTO: <a href={u('/services')}>our services</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What it's like to work with us</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><h3>You talk to the builders</h3><p>No account managers in between. The people you speak to are the people building it.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>You see it working</h3><p>Something you can open and try, early and often.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Looked after, and yours</h3><p>We host it, support it and keep it running for as long as you want us to. The code and data are always yours, so you're never stuck.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>No jargon</h3><p>Plain English in proposals, updates and invoices.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use AI</h2>
    <p>We use AI a lot, because it gets you results faster: prototypes in weeks, and more of your budget spent on the parts that matter. A person oversees it and checks everything before it reaches you, and we're open about where and how we use it.</p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>
